armGBA-pico patch to upstream armGBA (src/cpu/jit.c), MPL-2.0 like the file it changes.
Copyright (c) 2026 TheGammaSqueeze. Applied by build.sh to a copy in out/src.

The code buffer was the same size for every machine. For netplay the core runs a second machine
beside the first, both in one heap, and two buffers of the full size do not fit beside two
cartridge buffers: the host now says how much a machine's code buffer gets (armgbaHostCodeSize),
at most what it got before. A smaller buffer only fills, and throws its code away, sooner.

--- a/src/cpu/jit.c
+++ b/src/cpu/jit.c
@@ -2661,6 +2661,12 @@
 	jit->codeSize = CODE_SIZE;
 	jit->code = jitHostAllocCode(&jit->codeSize);
 	if (!jit->code) {
+#elif defined(ARMGBA_HOST_CODE_MIB)
+	// The host may give a machine less than the most (a second machine sharing its memory).
+	extern size_t armgbaHostCodeSize(size_t most);
+	jit->codeSize = armgbaHostCodeSize(CODE_SIZE);
+	jit->code = mmap(NULL, jit->codeSize, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE | PROT_EXEC, MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANONYMOUS, -1, 0);
+	if (jit->code == MAP_FAILED) {
 #else
 	jit->code = mmap(NULL, CODE_SIZE, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE | PROT_EXEC, MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANONYMOUS, -1, 0);
 	jit->codeSize = CODE_SIZE;
